@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - routes/web.ts
+  - src/app.ts
+  - app/Providers/AuthProvider.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Policies/PostPolicy.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+  - tests/PostAgentTools.test.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/claude-fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T17:22:49.387Z }
+---
+
+# Expose posts to assistants over MCP
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write with their own AI assistants and want them to search the blog
+and draft posts on it. We do not want a chatbot in the blog, a second copy of
+either feature, or protocol code of our own to maintain.
+
+## Decision
+
+Two existing routes declare `agent` metadata in `routes/web.ts` and become
+tools; `@guren/plugin-mcp` serves them at `/mcp`.
+
+| Tool | Route | Read-only |
+|---|---|---|
+| `posts_search` | `QUERY /posts/search` (`posts.search`) | yes |
+| `posts_store` | `POST /posts` (`posts.store`) | no |
+
+- A tool call re-enters the application as a request to its route, so the
+  body schema, the `auth` middleware and the `PostPolicy` check in
+  `PostController` are the ones the website runs. `posts_store` takes its
+  author from the authenticated user, never from the input.
+- Tool names use underscores (`agent.toolName`) because some assistants drop
+  a tool whose name contains a dot. The route names keep their dots.
+- `/mcp` requires a bearer token. Tokens live in the `api_tokens` table
+  through `DatabaseApiTokenStore`, which `AuthProvider` registers with
+  `auth.useTokens()`. A token carries tool scopes (`tool:<name>`,
+  `tools:read`, `tools:*`); the default `*` ability grants no tool.
+- Ops issue tokens from a terminal:
+  `bunx guren token:issue --name <label> --user <id> --tools posts_search,posts_store --expires 30d`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A change to a route's validation or authorization reaches the tool with no
+  further work; `bunx guren tool:list` and `bunx guren check` show and verify
+  what is exposed.
+- `posts_store` answers the way the form does, with a redirect to the new
+  post, which the assistant reads as `HTTP 303 (Location: /posts/<id>)`. It
+  advertises no output schema, which `guren check` reports as a warning.
+- A deploy has to apply the `api_tokens` migration before `/mcp` can verify
+  a token.
+- Users cannot create or revoke tokens themselves, and tool calls are neither
+  approved by a human nor written to an audit log. The plugin's default rate
+  limit applies, per token and per process.
